    <dcat:dataset>
      <dcat:Dataset rdf:about="https://ontology.energy-guard.eu/rea#Dataset_Buildings_monthly_heat_series_ARCGIS_Server">
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">Monthly heat consumption updates from 01.2021 to the current month for the 4,845 multi-apartment buildings that don't share a heat generator, pulled from the georiga ArcGIS REST service to extend the historical heating dataset.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:publisher rdf:resource="https://ontology.energy-guard.eu/pilots#REA"/>
        <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">Buildings monthly heat series - ARCGIS Server</dcterms:title>
        <schema1:variableMeasured rdf:resource="https://ontology.energy-guard.eu/rea#Buildings_monthly_heat_series_ARCGIS_Server__01_2021_current_month_current_year"/>
        <schema1:variableMeasured rdf:resource="https://ontology.energy-guard.eu/rea#Buildings_monthly_heat_series_ARCGIS_Server__Adrese"/>
        <schema1:variableMeasured rdf:resource="https://ontology.energy-guard.eu/rea#Buildings_monthly_heat_series_ARCGIS_Server__Kadastra_Nr"/>
        <skos:note>These are the monthly updates for the heating consumption time series data. | They come from https://georiga.lv/server/rest/services/REA/MapServer/0/query?where=1%3D1&amp;outFields=*&amp;returnGeometry=true&amp;f=json. | It is based on the previous dataset, but the updates are not for every building - they are from the residential multi-apartment that not share heat generator, i.e. the cadastral numbers/building (4845) of https://epuntuagr.sharepoint.com/:x:/r/sites/EnergyGuardConsortium/Document%20Library/5-Work%20Packages%20Working%20Folders/WP4%20-%20EnergyGuard%20TEF%20AI%20Development%20Sandbox%20and%20Integration/T4.5/Buildings%20list%20for%20DT.xlsx?d=w4abad13559c341549c714c7c9ab36303&amp;csf=1&amp;web=1&amp;e=SExlJV. | The updates from georiga sevrer will enrich the dataset, by adding the new monthly value to the historical ones.</skos:note>
        <eg:storedInDatabaseTable>public.f_tsdata</eg:storedInDatabaseTable>
      </dcat:Dataset>
    </dcat:dataset>
